# Cloud Functions Environment Configuration

## File Location
`functions/.env`

## Required Variables

```env
# Gmail Configuration (Use App Password, not regular password)
GMAIL_USER=your-email@gmail.com
GMAIL_PASSWORD=abcd efgh ijkl mnop

# Firebase Configuration
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project-id
FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY=-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----
...
-----END PRIVATE KEY-----

# Optional
NODE_ENV=production
FUNCTION_REGION=us-central1
```

## How to Get Gmail App Password

1. Go to [Google Account Security](https://myaccount.google.com/security)
2. Enable 2-Step Verification
3. Go to [App Passwords](https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords)
4. Select "Mail" and "Windows Computer"
5. Copy the 16-character password
6. Use this in `GMAIL_PASSWORD`

## Email Sender Configuration

By default, emails are sent from the Gmail account specified in `GMAIL_USER`.

You can customize:
- Sender name: Modify in Cloud Functions code
- Email templates: Edit HTML in functions/index.js
- From address: Change GMAIL_USER in .env

## Testing Locally

```bash
# Install Firebase emulator
firebase emulators:start --only functions

# This loads .env automatically
```

## Deployment

When deploying to Firebase:

1. Set environment variables:
```bash
firebase functions:config:set gmail.user="your-email@gmail.com" gmail.password="your-app-password"
```

2. Or update `.env` and deploy:
```bash
firebase deploy --only functions
```

## Troubleshooting

**Error: "Invalid credentials"**
- Check GMAIL_USER is correct
- Verify GMAIL_PASSWORD is the App Password, not regular password
- Ensure 2FA is enabled on Gmail account

**Error: "Less secure app"**
- Gmail may block Firebase
- Use [Gmail App Password](https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords) instead

**Emails not sending**
- Check Cloud Function logs: `firebase functions:log`
- Verify Firestore is accessible
- Check email address is valid

## Rate Limiting

Email sending has built-in limits:
- OTP: 5 minutes expiry
- Resend: 30 second cooldown
- Max attempts: 3 per OTP
- Verification: 24 hour link expiry

## Security

- Store `.env` in `.gitignore`
- Never commit credentials
- Use App Passwords, not account passwords
- Rotate passwords regularly
